      "parsed_output": {
        "evidence": "Unpatched run output: \"resolved file : /tmp/pov-ext-...-root/secret.txt\", \"bytes served : TOP-SECRET-DO-NOT-SERVE-8f3a1c2b\", \"VULNERABLE ...\", EXIT=0. Confirmed regression by temporarily changing ExternalResourceHandler to `UriPath.canonical(path.replace('\\\\','/'))`: getResource() returned null and the same command exited 1; patch then reverted (product source clean). Root cause: UriPath.canonical only recognizes '/' as separator (verified: canonical(\"/..\\\\secret.txt\") returns the string unchanged) while ExternalResource -> StringUtils.cleanPath converts '\\' to '/' and collapses '..'.",
        "expected_vulnerable_behavior": "On unpatched code the POV drives the real spark.resource.ExternalResourceHandler.getResource(String) with base=<tmp>/public and attacker path \"/..\\secret.txt\". The handler returns a non-null ExternalResource that resolves to <tmp>/secret.txt (outside base), and reading resource.getInputStream() returns the secret file's bytes. The runner prints \"VULNERABLE\" and exits 0. A correct patch (normalize/reject backslash traversal, or validate the resolved path stays within base) makes getResource() return null, so the POV prints \"traversal blocked\" and exits 1.",
        "notes": "POV exercises real project classes directly (ExternalResourceHandler.getResource, ExternalResource.getPath/getInputStream) via a trivial subclass needed only to reach the protected getResource(String); no product code or normal tests were modified. run_pov.sh compiles the project (mvn -DskipTests compile if target/classes is missing), locates slf4j-api and javax.servlet-api from ~/.m2, compiles the POV into .security-pipeline/pov/out, and runs it. The temp layout (base dir + secret sibling) is created by the POV itself, so it is self-contained and deterministic. Command runs inside /workspace/repo in the project container.",
        "pov_command": "bash .security-pipeline/pov/run_pov.sh",
        "pov_path": ".security-pipeline/pov/PovExternalTraversal.java",
        "regression_hint": "After a correct fix, `bash .security-pipeline/pov/run_pov.sh` must exit non-zero (getResource returns null / resource stays within base). The fix should either normalize backslashes to forward slashes before UriPath.canonical(), have canonical treat '\\' as a separator, or verify the final resolved file's canonical path is contained within the configured base directory. Any of these blocks the \"/..\\secret.txt\" traversal and flips the POV to exit 1.",
        "status": "pov_created",
        "summary": "ExternalResourceHandler's only traversal defense, UriPath.canonical(), treats only '/' as a path separator, so a request path using backslashes (\"/..\\secret.txt\") passes through unchanged. ExternalResource's constructor then runs the combined path through StringUtils.cleanPath(), which converts '\\' to '/' and normalizes the resulting '..' segments, escaping the configured base directory. The handler returns a live resource whose InputStream leaks a file located outside the served root — a CWE-022 path traversal."
      }
