        "diff_review": "Product change is confined to ExternalResourceHandler.getResource(): `path = UriPath.canonical(path.replace('\\\\','/'))` plus a `if (path == null) return null;` guard. Root cause verified in source: UriPath.canonical() only treats '/' as a separator (leaving '/..\\\\secret.txt' unchanged), while ExternalResource->StringUtils.cleanPath() converts '\\\\'->'/' and collapses '..', escaping the base dir. Normalizing '\\\\'->'/' before canonical() turns the attack into '/../secret.txt', which canonical() rejects (returns null on '..' above root). The null guard is required because canonical() can now legitimately return null. Change is a no-op for legitimate forward-slash paths. Does not remove functionality or add unrelated behavior. The pov.diff only adds the self-contained POV harness and compiled artifacts under .security-pipeline/pov/; no product code or existing tests were modified by the POV. The only test change is an added regression test (testGetResource_whenPathUsesBackslashTraversal_thenReturnNull) asserting getResource(\"/..\\\\secret.txt\") returns null.",
